-their exact identity through expected `D_root`; TypeScript contains no second
-full-value root table. `RefDigest` has exactly the two shown fields; every
-shown object rejects unknown keys and every success/selection is recursively
-frozen. The reason and refusal-code unions are exhaustive. The existing `VerifiedProductArtifact`,
-`VerifyProductRequest`, and exact Public operation-family request, result, and
-refusal schemas remain byte/schema/semantic compatible. The port is a package
-proof seam, not a new
-`PublicFunctionDefinition`, Public operation, mode, runtime selector, or
-capability.
