-### 15.1 Immutable archive identity
-
-Let `C` be the exact reviewed docs commit or exact built-and-proved
-implementation commit. It retains its reviewed tree and expected remote-main
-parent `O`; delivery never recreates it under another commit identity. Let
-`R_a` be a distinct archive commit with `tree(R_a) = tree(C)` and
-`parent(R_a) = C`. All new archive refs use the full candidate OID `C`, not
-`R_a`:
-
-```text
-refs/heads/archive/t287-s1-docs-<accepted|rejected>-<full-oid>
-refs/heads/archive/t287-s1-dev<N>-<accepted|rejected>-<full-oid>
-```
-
-Here `<full-oid>` is exactly the 40-hex OID of `C`.
-
-Every archive creation is a compare-and-swap from the all-zero OID to exact
-`R_a`. An existing ref, nonzero old value, force move, deletion, or reuse
-refuses.
-
-Canonical `ArchiveMetadataCore` is the canonical commit-message block of
-`R_a`, never a file in its tree. It binds `C`'s full OID, parent, tree, and
-patch digest; subject kind and verdict; candidate version when applicable;
-artifact and proof coordinates when applicable; and governing design/law
-coordinates. It contains neither `R_a`'s own OID, archive ref, delivery
-receipt, nor remote observation. Its domain-separated digest therefore excludes
-the commit that encloses it. A candidate parent/tree/patch mismatch refuses
-before `R_a` is created.
